{"duration_api_ms":64552,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c3bac439-8732-4643-a36a-96c31d743c21","total_cost_usd":0.26824939999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17274,"cache_read_input_tokens":133457,"output_tokens":7757,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":242},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17274},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":28236,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3640,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":7757,"cacheReadInputTokens":133457,"cacheCreationInputTokens":17274,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26824939999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":242,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":17274,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NN5FLxEi3tdHP2guTvw2hS","tool_input":{"command":"D=.dark-factory/runs/1ee862c9-32dc-47f9-8188-ac761f888195/artifacts/ARCHITECTURE; mkdir -p $D\ncat > $D/design.md <<'EOF'\n# Design — Add `multiply(a, b)` to `app_int.main`, with a test\n\n## Summary\nAdd one pure function, `multiply`, to the existing module `src/app_int/main.py`\n(import path `app_int.main`), mirroring the existing `add` function exactly in\nshape. Add a pytest test to the existing `tests/test_main.py`. No other file\nchanges. This is the smallest change that satisfies AC-1..AC-11.\n\n## Current state (verified in repo)\n- `src/app_int/main.py` — module docstring, `from __future__ import annotations`,\n  then `health_check() -> dict[str, str]` and `add(a: int, b: int) -> int`, each\n  with a one-line docstring.\n- `tests/test_main.py` — `from app_int.main import add, health_check` plus\n  `test_health_check_reports_ok` and `test_add_returns_the_sum`.\n- `pyproject.toml` — `dependencies = []`; ruff rules `E, F, I, UP, B`,\n  line length 100; package built from `src/app_int`.\n- The task text says `app_int/main.py`; per BA assumption A1 this is\n  `src/app_int/main.py`. No new top-level `app_int/` directory is created.\n\n## Affected components\n| File | Change | Owner (write scope) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app_int/main.py` | Append new function `multiply` after `add` | DEVELOPMENT (`src/**`) |\n| `tests/test_main.py` | Extend import; add test function(s) for `multiply` | QA (`tests/**`) |\n\nImportant sequencing note: the DEVELOPMENT role's write scope is `src/**` only,\nso the Developer must **not** touch `tests/`. The test required by AC-7 is\nauthored by QA (write scope `tests/**`), which runs after DEVELOPMENT. The\nDeveloper may verify behaviour locally (e.g. with an ad-hoc `python -c` check)\nbut must leave no files outside `src/`.\n\n## Interface (new)\n`multiply` in module `app_int.main`:\n- Name: `multiply` — public, module-level, defined with `def` (not a lambda,\n  not an alias), so `inspect.signature` reports parameters cleanly.\n- Parameters: exactly two, named `a` then `b`, both positional-or-keyword\n  (same kind as `add`), no defaults, no `*args`/`**kwargs`. (AC-2)\n- Annotations: `a: int`, `b: int`, return `int` — identical to `add`. (AC-6)\n- Docstring: one line, same style as `add`, e.g. \"Return the product of two\n  integers.\" (AC-6)\n- Behaviour: returns the arithmetic product `a * b` using Python's built-in\n  multiplication operator. No validation, no type coercion, no error handling\n  (BA A2/A3). This inherently satisfies AC-3, AC-4, AC-5.\n\nPlacement: immediately after `add`, separated by two blank lines (PEP 8 / ruff\nE30x). Do not reorder or modify `health_check` or `add`. (AC-8)\n\n### Note on annotations and `from __future__ import annotations`\nThe module keeps `from __future__ import annotations`, so at runtime\n`inspect.signature(multiply).parameters[\"a\"].annotation` is the *string*\n`\"int\"`, not the class `int` (same as for `add` today). Tests that check AC-6\nshould use `typing.get_type_hints(multiply)` (which resolves to `int`) or accept\neither `int` or `\"int\"`. The Developer must not remove the future import to\n\"fix\" this — that would change the module for no requirement.\n\n## Test design (QA)\nIn `tests/test_main.py`:\n- Extend the existing import to `from app_int.main import add, health_check, multiply`\n  (keep names sorted so ruff `I` passes).\n- Add at least one test, e.g. `test_multiply_returns_the_product`, asserting\n  `multiply(2, 3) == 6`. Recommended additional assertions/tests for zero and\n  negatives (`multiply(0, 5) == 0`, `multiply(-2, 3) == -6`,\n  `multiply(-2, -3) == 6`), and optionally a signature/annotation/docstring\n  check per the note above.\n- Leave the two existing tests unchanged. (AC-7, AC-8)\n\n## Data flow\nCaller → `multiply(a, b)` → `a * b` → returned int. Pure function; no state,\nI/O, or side effects.\n\n## Sequencing\n1. DEVELOPMENT: add `multiply` to `src/app_int/main.py`; run\n   `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run pytest -q` (existing tests must still pass).\n2. QA: add the `multiply` test(s) to `tests/test_main.py`; run the quality gate.\n3. Quality gate: `uv run pytest -q` and `uv run ruff check .` both exit 0.\n   (AC-9, AC-10)\n\n## AC traceability\n| AC | Satisfied by |\n|---|---|\n| AC-1 | Public `def multiply` in `app_int.main` |\n| AC-2 | Params exactly `a`, `b`, no defaults/varargs |\n| AC-3, AC-4, AC-5 | Body returns `a * b` |\n| AC-6 | One-line docstring; `int` annotations on `a`, `b`, return |\n| AC-7 | QA test in `tests/test_main.py` importing from `app_int.main` |\n| AC-8 | `health_check`, `add`, and existing tests untouched |\n| AC-9, AC-10 | Ruff-clean code (import sort, blank lines, line length); tests pass |\n| AC-11 | No edits to `pyproject.toml` |\n\n## Tradeoffs / decisions\n- **Mirror `add` rather than generalise** (e.g. `numbers.Number`, `*args`):\n  requirements fix the domain to `int` and two operands; generalising adds\n  surface with no requirement behind it.\n- **Test lives in existing `tests/test_main.py`** rather than a new file: keeps\n  tests for `app_int.main` co-located; BA A4 suggests this file.\n- **No input validation**: `add` has none; `int * int` cannot overflow in\n  Python. Passing non-ints is unspecified behaviour and untested.\n\n## Open questions\nNone blocking.\nEOF\ncat > $D/constraints.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"constraints\": [\n    {\"id\": \"C-1\", \"description\": \"Add `multiply` only to the existing module `src/app_int/main.py` (import path `app_int.main`); do not create a new top-level `app_int/` directory or any new module. [AC-1, BA A1]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-2\", \"description\": \"`multiply` must be a module-level `def` with exactly two positional-or-keyword parameters named `a` and `b`, in that order, with no defaults, `*args`, or `**kwargs`. [AC-2]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-3\", \"description\": \"`multiply` must be annotated `a: int, b: int` and return `-> int`, and have a non-empty one-line docstring in the same style as `add`. [AC-6, R5]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-4\", \"description\": \"`multiply` must return `a * b` using the built-in operator, with no input validation, type coercion, or custom error handling. [AC-3, AC-4, AC-5, BA A2/A3]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-5\", \"description\": \"Do not modify `health_check`, `add`, the module docstring, or the `from __future__ import annotations` import in `src/app_int/main.py`. [AC-8, design decision]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-6\", \"description\": \"The DEVELOPMENT role writes only under `src/**`; it must not create or edit files under `tests/`. The `multiply` test is authored by QA in `tests/test_main.py`. [AC-7, role write scopes]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-7\", \"description\": \"The test for `multiply` must import it via `from app_int.main import ...`, keep the import sorted (ruff `I`), assert on return values, and leave `test_health_check_reports_ok` and `test_add_returns_the_sum` unchanged. Any annotation check must account for `from __future__ import annotations` (use `typing.get_type_hints` or accept the string `\\\"int\\\"`). [AC-6, AC-7, AC-8]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-8\", \"description\": \"Do not modify `pyproject.toml`; `[project].dependencies` must remain an empty list and no new runtime or dev dependencies are added. [AC-11, R9]\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-9\", \"description\": \"All changes must pass the quality gate: `uv run pytest -q` and `uv run ruff check .` both exit 0 (ruff rules E, F, I, UP, B; line length 100). [AC-9, AC-10]\"}\n  ]\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$D/constraints.json'))\" && git status --short","description":"Write design.md and constraints.json"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":7,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written `design.md` and `constraints.json` under `.dark-factory/runs/1ee862c9-32dc-47f9-8188-ac761f888195/artifacts/ARCHITECTURE/`. Nothing in the repository source was changed. Bash was denied, so I couldn't run a JSON or schema check on `constraints.json`. I wrote it by hand to match the schema: one `constraints` array, and each entry has only `id` and `description`.\n\n**The design:**\n- **What changes:** one new function, `multiply(a: int, b: int) -> int`, goes into `src/app_int/main.py` right after `add`. It has a one-line docstring and returns `a * b`, with no input checking. The task says `app_int/main.py`, but that file actually lives at `src/app_int/main.py`.\n- **Who writes the test:** the Developer can only write under `src/**`, so they must not touch `tests/`. QA, which can only write under `tests/**`, adds the `multiply` test to `tests/test_main.py` (needed for AC-7). QA adds `multiply` to the existing import and checks the zero and negative-number cases.\n- **Type-annotation check:** the module starts with `from __future__ import annotations`, so `inspect.signature` reports the type as the text `\"int\"` rather than `int` itself. A test checking AC-6 should use `typing.get_type_hints` or accept either form. The Developer must not remove that import to get around this.\n- **Coverage:** all 11 acceptance criteria are mapped to the design in a table. `constraints.json` has 9 constraints (C-1 to C-9), each pointing back to a criterion, a requirement or a design decision. They include leaving `pyproject.toml` alone, leaving `add` and `health_check` unchanged, and passing ruff.\n\nThere are no open questions that block the next step.","ttft_ms":2656,"type":"result","duration_ms":64792,"uuid":"8d48b18c-3078-4b58-86ac-ca1e0d4c84f0","ttft_stream_ms":1710,"time_to_request_ms":126,"first_content_frame_ms":1710,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
